## Upstream material

This project derives material from the following upstream works. Licences are
stated as verified for the versions actually used; the SPDX-JSON SBOM attached to
each GitHub release names the complete dependency inventory of the released
binary.

| Upstream work | Licence | What is derived | Distribution |
|---|---|---|---|
| HashiCorp `terraform-provider-scaffolding-framework` | MPL-2.0 | Entry point (`main.go`) and the provider build/serve pattern | Source and binary |
| `aminueza/terraform-provider-minio` (commit `0bce044`) | AGPL-3.0 | `.github/` CI and release YAML (workflow configuration only; no Go source code taken) | Repository configuration only, not compiled into the binary |
| Apache Gravitino OpenAPI specification (`docs/open-api/`) | Apache-2.0 | `internal/models` request/response shapes and the example payloads used in tests | Source and binary |
| HashiCorp Terraform plugin libraries | MPL-2.0 | `terraform-plugin-framework`, `terraform-plugin-framework-validators`, `terraform-plugin-go`, `terraform-plugin-log` and `terraform-plugin-testing` are compiled into the provider and its tests; `terraform-plugin-docs` is used at build time to generate `docs/` | Binary and build tooling |
| `github.com/jcmturner/gokrb5/v8` | Apache-2.0 | Kerberos SPNEGO authentication | Binary |

`github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto` appears in `go.mod` but not in `go list -deps .`: it is build
tooling only and is not linked into the released binary.

The `.github/` workflow configuration adapted from the AGPL-3.0 project above is
configuration, not linked or combined with the provider binary; the Go source of
this provider is not a derivative work of it.

The published identifiers are the Go module path
`github.com/gravitino/terraform-provider-gravitino` and the Terraform Registry
namespace `registry.terraform.io/caberdo/gravitino`; the source repository is
<https://github.com/caberdo/terraform-provider-gravitino>.

## Third-party dependencies

The complete dependency inventory, with versions and licences, is listed in the
SPDX-JSON SBOM generated by `anchore/sbom-action` in `.github/workflows/release.yml`
and attached to every GitHub release.

Apache Gravitino itself is not included in this distribution; the provider talks to
a Gravitino server over its REST API.
